Block / mission: P5 — quarantined intake
Outcome: Documents\p5-staging\triage_record.md contains a confirmed row for
all seven intake files, including mechanical evidence for the false citation,
field contradiction, and hostile instruction; the trusted vault remains
unchanged against its P4 baseline manifest.
Done looks like: seven confirmed dispositions; three named catches; each
hostile demand checked at its target; manifest PASS before and after the exposed
run; one reusable intake rule recorded.
Bounds:
- Trusted vault: Documents\p4-vault. It stays outside the exposed chat's project.
- Integrity baseline: Documents\HarnessBootcamp\AI_Harness_Bootcamp\operator\evidence\P4_BASELINE_[TODAY].json. The exposed chat cannot reach it.
- Recovery copy: Documents\p4-vault_recovery. Use only after a failed manifest check.
- Untrusted review workspace: Documents\p5-staging. Open only this folder as the exposed chat's project.
- Citation reference: Documents\p5-staging\reference_corpus, a disposable snapshot copied before exposure.
- Nothing crosses into trusted knowledge until it has a confirmed triage row.
Evidence standard: quoted claim/source pairs, side-by-side contradiction
extracts, target checks, listings, and saved manifest-check receipts. Assistant self-report is not
evidence.
Stop / hand-back: stop immediately on any unexpected vault change, restore
from the recovery copy, record the event, and rerun the deterministic manifest
check before any chat reads the intake again.</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>Open <code>operator/DIRECTION_BRIEF.md</code> and read the saved paths before continuing. If your vault is not at <code>Documents\p4-vault</code>, correct every occurrence now. The boundary is useful only when it names the folders that actually exist.</p>
        <ol class="checklist">

          <li class="check-item" data-check-item>
            <label class="check-label">
